-- Codex Insurance Limited -- Policy of Insurance
--
-- Encodes: given the fact pattern of a single hospitalization, is the claim it
-- gives rise to covered under the policy?
--
-- Two simplifications, both directed by the task brief rather than inferred:
--   * Clauses 1.1(1) [the agreement is signed] and 1.1(2) [the premium has been
--     paid, on time] are assumed always satisfied and are therefore not modelled
--     as facts on Claim at all.
--   * Every date/time below other than the claimant's age is a NUMBER of months
--     elapsed since the policy's effective date (never an absolute DATE), so no
--     date arithmetic is needed anywhere in this file -- only comparison against
--     the 6-month and 7-month anniversaries named in § 1.3, and the 12-month term
--     named in § 3.6.
--
-- Sections below are labelled to match the source contract, but *defined* in
-- dependency order: § 1.3 first (the wellness-visit condition), then § 1.2
-- (cancelation, which reads § 1.3's result), then § 1.1 (in effect, which reads
-- both), then § 2.1 (the exclusions, which are independent of all of the above),
-- and finally the combined `covered` test that § 1.1 and § 2.1 together decide.

§§ `The fact pattern of a hospitalization claim`

-- § 2.1 excludes a hospitalization only when it "arises directly or indirectly
-- out of" one of four enumerated activities. That is a single-cause
-- classification -- what did this hospitalization arise out of? -- and not a
-- checklist of the claimant's unrelated attributes: merely being a serving
-- police officer, for instance, does not by itself make an unrelated injury
-- "arise out of" police service. So the cause is modelled as one closed
-- enumeration (the operative cause of the hospitalization) rather than as four
-- independent occupation/activity flags that could be checked off regardless of
-- causation.
DECLARE `Cause of Hospitalization` IS ONE OF
    `Skydiving`
    `Service in the Military`
    `Service as a Fire Fighter`
    `Service in the Police`
    `Not one of the enumerated excluded activities`

DECLARE Claim HAS
    -- § 1.1: when the hospitalization occurred, in months after the effective date
    `time of hospitalization`                            IS A NUMBER
    -- § 1.2: fraud, misrepresentation, or material withholding of information
    `fraud, misrepresentation, or material withholding`  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- § 1.3: when written confirmation of the wellness visit was supplied to the
    -- Company, in months after the effective date; NOTHING if no confirmation had
    -- been supplied as of the time of hospitalization
    `written confirmation supplied at`                   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    -- § 1.3: when the underlying wellness visit itself took place, in months
    -- after the effective date; NOTHING when not separately known (see NOTES.md
    -- for why this is tracked apart from the confirmation date, and why it goes
    -- unset in every one of this trial's nine claims)
    `wellness visit occurred at`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    -- § 2.1(1)-(4): what the sickness or accidental injury arose out of
    `cause of the hospitalization`                       IS A `Cause of Hospitalization`
    -- § 2.1(5): the claimant's age when hospitalized -- an absolute figure, the
    -- one time-like quantity the task brief exempts from "relative to the
    -- effective date"
    `age at the time of hospitalization`                 IS A NUMBER

§§ `1.3 -- the wellness-visit condition`

-- "... of a wellness visit ... occurring no later than the 6th month anniversary
-- of the effective date of this policy."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the wellness visit itself occurred in time` claim IS
    CONSIDER claim's `wellness visit occurred at`
    WHEN JUST t THEN t AT MOST 6
    OTHERWISE      TRUE   -- not separately known; not a fact any of the nine queries puts in issue

-- "No later than the 7th month anniversary ... you will supply us with written
-- confirmation ..."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `written confirmation was supplied by the 7th month anniversary` claim IS
    CONSIDER claim's `written confirmation supplied at`
    WHEN JUST t THEN t AT MOST 7
    OTHERWISE      FALSE

-- The compound condition named in § 1.3: confirmation on file by month 7, of a
-- visit that itself happened by month 6.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the wellness condition, taken as a whole, was satisfied` IF
        `written confirmation was supplied by the 7th month anniversary` claim
    AND `the wellness visit itself occurred in time` claim

-- § 1.1(3): "... is still pending or has been satisfied in a timely fashion ..."
-- If no confirmation has been supplied at all, the condition is merely "still
-- pending" for as long as the hospitalization being assessed occurs no later
-- than the 7-month deadline; from that deadline onward, silence is a failure.
-- If a confirmation *has* been supplied, that fact -- checked against §1.3's
-- full compound condition above -- is dispositive on its own, independent of
-- when the hospitalization itself falls.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `condition 1.3 is pending or has been satisfied in a timely fashion` claim IS
    CONSIDER claim's `written confirmation supplied at`
    WHEN JUST t THEN `the wellness condition, taken as a whole, was satisfied` claim
    OTHERWISE        claim's `time of hospitalization` AT MOST 7

§§ `1.2 -- cancelation`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the policy has been canceled` IF
        claim's `fraud, misrepresentation, or material withholding`
    OR  NOT (`condition 1.3 is pending or has been satisfied in a timely fashion` claim)
    OR  claim's `time of hospitalization` GREATER THAN 12   -- § 3.6: a one-year policy term

§§ `1.1 -- the policy in effect`

-- Clauses 1.1(1) and 1.1(2) (signature; premium paid) are assumed satisfied
-- throughout and are not modelled as facts -- see the file header.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the policy is in effect` IF
        `condition 1.3 is pending or has been satisfied in a timely fashion` claim
    AND NOT (`the policy has been canceled` claim)

§§ `2.1 -- general exclusions`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cause of the hospitalization is on the excluded list` claim IS
    CONSIDER claim's `cause of the hospitalization`
    WHEN `Skydiving`                                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Service in the Military`                        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Service as a Fire Fighter`                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Service in the Police`                           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Not one of the enumerated excluded activities`   THEN FALSE

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exclusion applies` IF
        `the cause of the hospitalization is on the excluded list` claim
    OR  claim's `age at the time of hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

§§ `3 -- general conditions with no operative effect on coverage`

-- § 3.1.1 ("insures You twenty-four (24) hours a day anywhere in the world") is a
-- coverage-affirming clause with no exceptions: there is no time-of-day or
-- location fact that could ever make it fail, so it needs no field and no rule.
-- §§ 3.2-3.5 (arbitration, governing law, currency, and premium-payment
-- mechanics) and Section 5 (the premium schedule) govern the relationship
-- between the parties but never decide whether a given hospitalization is
-- covered, so they are likewise not modelled.

§§ `Putting it together -- is a claim covered?`

-- § 1.1 conditions payment on the policy being in effect at the time of the
-- hospitalization; § 2.1 separately bars payment when an exclusion applies.
-- Both must clear for a claim to be covered.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE covered IF
        `the policy is in effect` claim
    AND NOT (`an exclusion applies` claim)
